+Setup needs an existing Node.js 24.12+ and Python 3.11+ interpreter; it uses only Python's standard-library TOML parser. Codex presents setup onboarding after installation. Setup registers the two bundled custom-agent definitions and their native config references, plus a description-only `pstack-general-purpose` role that leaves your existing default role intact. It stores your role choices in `$CODEX_HOME/pstack-for-codex/models.json`, defaulting to `~/.codex`. Re-run setup after an update or a prior-version restore to synchronize its owned agent files. Existing user edits stop replacement; role preferences are retained.
+
+Before removing the plugin, ask setup to unregister its managed agents. It removes only its unchanged agent files and owned role declarations; unrelated configuration and your model preferences remain. Then use `codex plugin remove pstack-for-codex@pstack-for-codex-local`. Native plugin removal does not run an agent-cleanup hook.
+
